# Frontend Styles

## Layout

- Prefer Bootstrap **`container` / `row` / `col-*`** for page and section layout.
- Prefer Bootstrap utilities (`gap-*`, `mb-*`, `d-*`, `align-items-*`) before custom CSS.
- Do not revive fixed `#root` widths or starter layouts that fight the grid.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="container py-4">
  <div className="row">
    <div className="col-12 col-md-8">...</div>
    <div className="col-12 col-md-4">...</div>
  </div>
</div>
```

## File organization

- One co-located style file per component that needs custom styles: `Component.tsx` + `Component.scss`.
- Import the SCSS from the component file.
- Shared tokens live in [`frontend/src/styles/_variables.scss`](frontend/src/styles/_variables.scss).
- Global Bootstrap entry is [`frontend/src/styles/main.scss`](frontend/src/styles/main.scss).
- Do not dump component-specific rules into `main.scss` or `_variables.scss`.

## Breakpoints / media queries

- Use Bootstrap breakpoint tokens from `_variables.scss` (`$breakpoint-sm` … `$breakpoint-xxl`, or `$grid-breakpoints`).
- When a component needs different styles per breakpoint, keep those media-query blocks in that component’s SCSS (or a dedicated partial imported by it)—not in global CSS.
- Prefer `min-width` queries matching Bootstrap’s mobile-first grid.

```scss
@use '../styles/variables' as *;

.card {
  padding: 1rem;

  @media (min-width: $breakpoint-md) {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
}
```

## Variables (centralize styling)

- Prefer SCSS variables / CSS custom properties from `_variables.scss` for colors, spacing, brand, breakpoints.
- Do not hard-code repeated hex/px values in component SCSS when a shared token exists or should be added.
- Add new shared tokens to `_variables.scss` when the same value is reused across components.

## Functions & reusability

- Use SCSS `@function` / `@mixin` for repeated calculations or patterns (e.g. spacing scale, focus ring, truncated text).
- Place shared mixins/functions in `frontend/src/styles/` (e.g. `_mixins.scss`, `_functions.scss`) and `@use` them from components.
- Keep mixins small and purposeful; do not wrap one-off styles.

## Nesting & scope

- Nest under a component root class (e.g. `.app`, `.product-card`) to avoid leaking styles.
- Keep nesting shallow (usually ≤3 levels).
- Override Bootstrap sparingly; prefer utilities + tokens first.
